From: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: fix Linux 6.6 optional APIs, broken RRM MIN macros, and STA isolation

- Fix intra-BSS STA isolation bypass in ap_data.c when IsolateInterStaTraffic == 1.
- Guard cmm_info.c MIN() macro and fix inverted > MIN() macros in rrm.c / rrm_tlv.c via min_t().
- Update proc_ops (>= 5.6), ktime_get_real_ts64/rtc_time64_to_tm (>= 5.0), netif_rx (>= 5.18),
  and dma_set_mask/dma_set_coherent_mask (>= 5.18), plus stray parenthesis in rt_proc.c.

Signed-off-by: sKyissKy <29267720+sKyissKy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/embedded/ap/ap_data.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/embedded/ap/ap_data.c
@@ -3970,8 +3970,10 @@
 				to_os = TRUE;
 				to_air = FALSE;
 
-				if (pMbss->IsolateInterStaTraffic == 1)
+				if (pMbss->IsolateInterStaTraffic == 1) {
+					to_os = FALSE;
 					to_air = FALSE;
+				}
 			} else {
 				/*
 					STAs in different SSID, default send to os and not to air
